# FITMATCH_QA_SIMULATOR_ID
# FITMATCH_QA_DERIVED_DATA

# All required for opt-in authenticated development DB smoke.
# Set through your local secret/environment mechanism, not a tracked file.
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_URL
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_PUBLIC_KEY
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_DEDICATED_USERS
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_USER_A_TOKEN
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_USER_A_ID
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_USER_B_TOKEN
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_USER_B_ID
# Additional normal session tokens for the real Swift SDK integration.
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_USER_A_REFRESH_TOKEN
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_USER_B_REFRESH_TOKEN
# Full authenticated domain cases require verified exact development seeds.
# FITMATCH_QA_DB_CASE_MANIFEST
# Runner supplies FITMATCH_QA_AUTH_RUN_ID / FITMATCH_QA_AUTH_OUTPUT per execution.
# Only the exact hnkplvyegonlhumlejst.supabase.co HTTPS host is accepted.
# DEDICATED_USERS must explicitly attest 1; both users must be disposable QA accounts.

# Standalone Swift interrupted-run cleanup only. Never put credentials in this file.
# FITMATCH_QA_AUTH_LEDGER=<absolute original Swift ledger path>
# FITMATCH_QA_AUTH_RUN_ID=<original ledger UUID; runner reads it for cleanup>
# Use: python3 scripts/release_qa.py cleanup --ledger <path> --output <new-directory>
